# SHELVED 2026-10-05. `8.tree` through `128.tree` each wrote `form u8` (and so on) over `fuse integer` with `self-type`,
# `actual-type`, `signed-type`, `bits` and `bits-minus-one`, and loaded no template: the one they were written for is
# `integer` in `native/<backend>/integer.tree`, which takes `self-type` and `unsigned-type`. So each fuse built nothing,
# and each module was an empty form. That went unsaid until a fuse was required to name a template the build has
# (compile/template.ts). Nothing loads these modules. The unsigned widths the library builds are in `../unsigned.tree`,
# from the template in `n.tree`.
